wn","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vamsadhara","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:38.196668+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple near Gudari in Rayagada district, Odisha, set in dense forest where three rivers meet: the Vamsadhara, Chauladhua and Phalaphalia. It is listed as a tourist spot in the district, and people from near and far visit during Shivaratri.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jeypore","nearest_airport_distance_km":143.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sansartali railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":27.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Minajhola), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"efe8b8c5-2307-4d21-ba4a-830c4596d2d9","name":"Soundararajaperumal temple, Thadikombu","deity":"Vishnu as Soundararaja Perumal","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Dindigul","town":"Thadikombu","latitude":10.43972,"longitude":77.95389,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kudakanar River","river_distance_km":0.4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:56.940052+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Dravidian-style Vishnu temple at Thadikombu near Dindigul, believed to have been built by Achyuta Deva Raya in the 16th century. Lakshmi is worshipped as Soundaravalli. It is known for life-size sculptures in the Ranga Mandapam and a separate shrine for Manmatha and Rati. The Brahmotsavam in Aadi is its main festival.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Madurai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":68.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Akkaraipatti railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Soundararajaperumal temple, Thadikombu), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":16},{"id":"f0621822-98ce-42f2-a18f-417abd08f130","name":"Nilkanth Dham","deity":"Swaminarayan","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Gujarat","district":"Narmada","town":"Gamdi","latitude":21.97129,"longitude":73.47222,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Narmada","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Swaminarayan temple and spiritual-cultural campus at Poicha, near the Narmada River in Gujarat. It is also called Nilkanthdham Poicha or Poicha Swaminarayan Mandir. By road it is roughly 80 km from Bharuch and 60 km from Vadodara, the latter being the nearest railway station and airport.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Vadodara Green Airport Harni","nearest_airport_distance_km":47.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Moriya railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Nilkanth Dham), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"f06dae2f-888e-453f-a42e-25230e5011c1","name":"Lokanatha Siva Temple","deity":"Shiva as Lokanatha","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Khordha","town":"Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation","latitude":20.24056,"longitude":85.83472,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dayaa River","river_distance_km":3.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:56.940052+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An 11th-century temple in Bhubaneswar, near the Lingaraja temple, regarded as a miniature prototype of it. It was buried up to its base until 1972, giving the name Amuha Deula, when an excavation exposed the entrance. The sanctum is empty; the Shiva attribution rests on local tradition and the wall sculpture. It is in poor condition.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":2.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhubaneswar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Lokanatha Siva Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Kalinga (Odisha)","construction_century":11},{"id":"f0739284-6ce2-4fe0-ba2b-ba9f72dabb90","name":"Bamleshwari Temple, Dongargarh","deity":"Bamleshwari — a form of Durga (the hilltop shrine is called Badi Bamleshwari)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Chhattisgarh","district":"Rajnandgaon","town":"Dongargarh","latitude":21.17944,"longitude":80.7525,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"Chaitra Navaratri and the autumn (Ashwin) Navaratri are the major festivals, with ritual lamps kindled for the nine days.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T20:05:50.919949+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-26T20:05:50.919949+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition holds that the childless King Veersen prayed here and his queen bore a son, Madansen; a second tradition ties the temple to King Vikramaditya. The temple is said to be about 2,200 years old, a traditional claim with no archaeological support.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":"The hilltop shrine (about 1,600 ft) is reached by roughly 1,000 steps or by a ropeway; ropeway hours were not confirmed, and safety incidents have been reported there in past years.","nearest_airport_name":"Swami Vivekananda Airport, Raipur","nearest_airport_distance_km":125,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Dongargarh Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Utsav (Government of India); Wikipedia (Bambleshwari Temple)","architecture_style":"Nagara","construction_century":null},{"id":"f16d9b99-1e4a-4950-a0c1-517c547073f2","name":"Apatsahayesvarar Temple, Alangudi","deity":"Apatsahayeswarar (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Navagraha Sthalam"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tiruvarur","town":"Alangudi","latitude":10.83,"longitude":79.41028,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cauvery delta","river_distance_km":5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; Thursdays, associated with Guru, are considered auspicious.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T11:47:03.785954+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"Known as the Guru Sthalam, this temple houses the Navagraha shrine for Guru (Jupiter), worshipped here in the form of Dakshinamurthy alongside the presiding Apatsahayeswarar. The principal linga is held to be swayambhu (self-manifested), so the temple's founding cannot be dated with certainty, though it is venerated in ten verses by the 7th-century Nayanar saint Tirugnana Sambandar in the Tevaram, making it a Paadal Petra Sthalam. The current structure was rebuilt in the 16th century under the Nayaks on an earlier Chola-era complex.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ஆபத்சகாயேஸ்வரர் கோயில், ஆலங்குடி","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Thanjavur Air Force Station","nearest_airport_distance_km":34.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nidamangalam Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Tevaram canon; local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Dravidian (Chola origins, Nayaka rebuilding)","construction_century":16},{"id":"f204d3eb-a454-400c-81ba-cb44a63bb19f","name":"Narasimha Temple, Bhubaneswar","deity":"Vishnu as Narasimha","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Khordha","town":"Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation","latitude":20.25306,"longitude":85.84333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dayaa River","river_distance_km":4.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A 14th-15th-century Narasimha shrine in the Gosagaresvara precinct at Bhubaneswar, dated from its architecture and sharing that temple's traditions. The four-armed image sits on a pedestal, holding conch and disc while killing a demon; the base carries rows of women in anjali mudra. The sanctum faces west.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":3.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhubaneswar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Narasimha Temple, Bhubaneswar), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":14},{"id":"f2105243-ae51-4d18-809a-eb336cb8841d","name":"Thirumandhamkunnu Temple","deity":"Bhadrakali (Thirumandhamkunnilamma), with Shiva as principal deity","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Malappuram","town":"Angadipuram","latitude":10.98018,"longitude":76.20163,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cherriya Puzha River","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T10:59:23.880063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A historic temple at Angadipuram, Malappuram district, once the capital of the Valluvanad rulers, whose official goddess was Thirumandhamkunnilamma. Warriors set out from here for the Mamankam festival, and a memorial platform for them stands at the entrance. Shiva is principal deity, while Bhadrakali and Ganesha are famed, notably for marriage offerings.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Calicut International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":32,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Angadipuram Raiway railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Thirumandhamkunnu Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"f284c349-0c18-4164-baa8-560a96b8bf34","name":"Banashankari Amma Temple","deity":"Banashankari (Shakambhari), form of Parvati","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Bagalkote","town":"Banashankari","latitude":15.88722,"longitude":75.705,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Malaprabha River","river_distance_km":1.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:56.940052+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A goddess temple at Cholachagudda near Badami, in the Tilakaranya forest, where the deity Banashankari or Shakambhari is seen as a form of Parvati. The original temple was built by the Badami Chalukyas of the 7th century, who held her as tutelary deity. The annual jatre in January or February includes a boat festival and a chariot procession.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Hubballi Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":89.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Lakhmapur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Banashankari Amma Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":7},{"id":"f2d3499e-f8ff-480e-8109-8e3eaca50898","name":"Thirukkadigai","deity":"Vishnu as Lakshmi Narasimhar","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Ranipet","town":"Sholinghur","latitude":13.0885,"longitude":79.4184,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Nandi River","river_distance_km":2.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:38.937899+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Divya Desam in Sholinghur, praised in the Divya Prabandham, with Vishnu as Lakshmi Narasimhar. Separate shrines to Narasimha, Bhaktavatsala Perumal and Hanuman sit on the larger hill, at its base and on the smaller hill. It follows the Tenkalai tradition and is run by the state endowments board.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":62,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Thalangai railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":9.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Thirukkadigai), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"f2fce6e8-2581-4c62-a2d2-57292579b3af","name":"Mukteswara Temple, Bhubaneswar","deity":"Shiva (Mukteshwara)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Kalinga architecture landmark"],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Khurda","town":"Bhubaneswar","latitude":20.2427,"longitude":85.84039,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dayaa River","river_distance_km":3.4,"best_season_notes":"The Mukteswar Dance Festival, an annual Odissi dance and music festival, is held here in winter.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T08:41:30.569832+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built around 950–975 CE, this compact temple is considered the earliest major work of the Somavamshi dynasty period, marking — per art historians including Percy Brown — the culmination of earlier Kalinga temple development and the start of a century of architectural experimentation that led to Rajarani and Lingaraj. It is celebrated above all for its ornate free-standing torana (arched gateway), thought to show Buddhist architectural influence. This dating rests on stylistic analysis rather than inscriptional proof — scholarly consensus, not epigraphic certainty.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":3.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhubaneswar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Art-historical scholarship (Percy Brown and others); Wikipedia","architecture_style":"Kalinga style, 10th century CE, celebrated for compact ornate carving and its torana","construction_century":10},{"id":"f36cfe5b-8ac2-45c0-a1ca-5dfa4fb61863","name":"Yogadhyan Badri Temple","deity":"Vishnu (meditating form)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Panch Badri"],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Chamoli","town":"Pandukeshwar","latitude":30.63323,"longitude":79.55035,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Alaknanda River","river_distance_km":0,"best_season_notes":"Accessible for most of the year via the Badrinath highway; becomes the effective seat of worship each winter when Badrinath itself closes.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T08:35:20.91066+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the five Panch Badri shrines to Vishnu. Every winter, when Badrinath Temple closes under snow, its idol of Vishnu is brought down and worshipped here instead. Tradition holds this is where King Pandu — father of the Pandavas — meditated seeking atonement for accidentally killing a sage who had taken the form of a mating deer, and where the Pandava princes were later born. Vishnu is worshipped here in a seated, meditating (yog dhyan) pose, in a temple built in the Dravidian style despite its Himalayan setting.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"योगध्यान बद्री मंदिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":140.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":null,"nearest_railway_distance_km":null,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"f386979f-92b4-4a44-bce4-4d58cf3d0a04","name":"Pancha Mukha Anjaneyar Temple, NGO Colony, Tiruvallur","deity":"Panchamukha Anjaneyar (five-faced Hanuman)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tiruvallur","town":"NGO Colony, Tiruvallur","latitude":13.14,"longitude":79.905,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cooum River","river_distance_km":3,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb, or around Hanuman Jayanti.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A five-faced Hanuman shrine in the NGO Colony locality of Tiruvallur town.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":32.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruvallur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"f3ef8295-68f0-469c-b8c4-500851e3ef43","name":"Harishankar Temple","deity":"Vishnu and Shiva (Harihara)","sampradaya":null,"significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Balangir","town":"Chhanchanabahali","latitude":20.85441,"longitude":82.86061,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Bondesara Nadi River","river_distance_km":8.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:38.196668+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple on the slopes of the Gandhamardhan hills in Bolangir district, Odisha, connected with both Vishnu and Shiva. It is known for its natural setting and a stream flowing over granite, which visitors find peaceful. The Nrusinghanath temple lies on the opposite side of the hills, with ancient Buddhist ruins on the plateau between them.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Swami Vivekananda Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":121.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Lakhna railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":24.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Harishankar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"f42d1a6c-e757-42c0-81d6-6ebf8cd553d6","name":"Govardhana Peetham, Puri","deity":"Sharada / Jagannath","sampradaya":"Smartha","significance":["Char Peetham"],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Puri","town":"Puri","latitude":19.8095,"longitude":85.8318,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The Bay of Bengal shore and the temple tanks are both within walking distance.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Bay of Bengal","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Dec–Feb. Sits beside the Jagannath temple, so the two are usually visited together — the same Odisha cyclone-season caution (Oct–Nov) applies to both.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T13:44:40.752775+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"The eastern Amnaya peetham, established by Adi Shankaracharya and associated with the Rig Veda. Its mahavakya is Prajnanam Brahma — \"consciousness is Brahman\" — and its first acharya in the traditional account was Padmapada, one of Shankara's four principal disciples.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ଗୋବର୍ଧନ ପୀଠ","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":49.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Puri railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"f443c65d-c91b-42e4-b171-e91182b972f6","name":"Mundaka Kanni Amman Temple, Mylapore","deity":"Mundaka Kanni Amman (Devi)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Mylapore","latitude":13.0342,"longitude":80.268,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_di