ipedia (Tarakeshwara Temple, Hangal), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"f496b5e6-486a-4f0f-bb39-7225fd989396","name":"Adi Srinivasa Perumal Temple","deity":"Vishnu as Adi Srinivasa Perumal","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Dharmapuri","town":"Dharmapuri","latitude":12.1386,"longitude":78.2577,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ponnaiyar River","river_distance_km":13.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:59.708182+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Vishnu temple at the foot of a hill in Mookanur, Dharmapuri district, Tamil Nadu, built in the Dravidian style and believed to be of Pallava origin. It follows the Vaikhanasa agama and has no Ganesha shrine. It is counted among the 108 Abhimana Kshethram and is the family deity of many local Brahmin and Gounder families.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Salem Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":44.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Dharmapuri railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":11.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Adi Srinivasa Perumal Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"f4ce8d36-b7de-4219-a704-64ff8232113e","name":"Ram Mandir, Ayodhya","deity":"Rama","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Sapta Puri"],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Ayodhya","town":"Ayodhya","latitude":26.7955,"longitude":82.1944,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The Sarayu river and its ghats run along the edge of town.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Free meals near the temple from trusts such as Shri Ram Rasoi and ISKCON's Anna Daan seva (not yet confirmed as the temple trust's own scheme)","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.5,"nearest_river_name":"Sarayu","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Nov and Feb–Mar are the clearest weeks, avoiding the Dec–Jan north Indian fog belt; Ram Navami (Mar/Apr) and Diwali see the largest crowds.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-05T18:23:31.36475+00:00","sthala_purana":"Revered as the birthplace (janmabhoomi) of Rama. The site was long contested between Hindu and Muslim communities and was the subject of a decades-long legal dispute, resolved by the Supreme Court of India in 2019; construction of the present temple began in 2020 and the sanctum was consecrated (pran pratishtha) in January 2024.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"श्री राम मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":"06:30:00","morning_closes_at":"12:00:00","evening_opens_at":"14:30:00","evening_closes_at":"22:00:00","timings_notes":"Doors close 12–2pm for a private bhog to Ram Lalla. Aartis: Mangala 4:30am, Shringar 6:30am, Sandhya 7pm, Shayan 10pm.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Prayagraj Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":160,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Ayodhya Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition, not a single classical Sanskrit text","architecture_style":"Modern","construction_century":21},{"id":"f5320209-a6fe-4d07-aa0d-78cb78b1c1b5","name":"Ghrishneshwar Temple","deity":"Shiva as Ghrishneshwar (Jyotirlinga)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar","town":"Ellora","latitude":20.02497,"longitude":75.16992,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Khadki River","river_distance_km":10.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple in Verul village near Ellora, counted among the twelve Jyotirlinga shrines. It lies about 1.5 km from the Ellora Caves and 30 km north-west of Aurangabad, and is a nationally protected site. It is mentioned in the Shiva Purana, Skanda Purana, Ramayana and Mahabharata.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":29.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Daulatabad railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":12.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Ghrishneshwar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"f56cd792-b5a4-4ac2-bf4c-f7b8a29d0b30","name":"Boro Maa Kali Temple, Naihati","deity":"Kali (Raksha Kali / Shamshan Kali)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Hooghly","town":"Hugli-Chuchura","latitude":22.8886,"longitude":88.41434,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_con