sed Shiva temple in Magaral village, Kanchipuram district, with Parvati as Tribuvananayagi. A five-tier gopuram faces the main shrine. Cholas are believed to have built the first complex, and the present masonry dates to the 16th century. It stands on the northern bank of the Cheyyar river.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":54.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Walajabad railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":11.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Thirumakaraleeswarar temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":16},{"id":"f5896dbf-05ff-4e79-8403-b58abfb8448b","name":"Chaya Someswara Temple","deity":"Shiva as Chaya Someshwara","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Nalgonda","town":"Panagal","latitude":17.07747,"longitude":79.29528,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:38.937899+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"A mid-11th-century trikutalayam in Panagal built under the Kunduru Chodas, with three sanctums for Shiva, Vishnu and Surya sharing one mandapam. Its pillars are carved with epic scenes. According to the article, pillars cast a steady shadow on the lingam, giving the temple its name. Maha Shivaratri draws pilgrims.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_clos