in verse by both Nammalvar and Tirumangai Alvar. Tradition holds the sage Hareetha performed long penance to Vishnu on the banks of a nearby river, and was rewarded at the start of Kali Yuga with Vishnu's appearance and counsel (thirumozhi, \"sacred words\") — giving the site its name.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"തിരുമൂഴിക്കുളം ശ്രീ ലക്ഷ്മണ പെരുമാള്‍ ക്ഷേത്രം","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":9.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Angamali (Kaladi) railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Nalayira Divya Prabandham; local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"f5ff3254-93bc-460d-a2ba-dcaf7ef94a0e","name":"Kukke Subramanya Temple","deity":"Subramanya (Murugan)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Dakshina Kannada","town":"Subrahmanya (Kukke)","latitude":12.6167,"longitude":75.6167,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Temple-run Annadana hall — free vegetarian lunch and dinner daily to all visitors, no coupon or payment needed","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.1,"nearest_river_name":"Dakshina (Kumaradhara)","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Dec for Champa Shashti/Subramanya Shashti; otherwise Oct–Feb, avoiding the region's heavy monsoon.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:20:34.20482+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:00.624755+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition holds this is one of the sites established by Parashurama, and the spot where the serpent-king Vasuki took refuge from Garuda; Subramanya is worshipped here as lord of all serpents. The temple is especially known for Sarpa Samskara and Ashlesha Bali rites performed for those believing themselves affected by sarpa dosha (astrological affliction linked to serpents).","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ಕುಕ್ಕೆ ಸುಬ್ರಹ್ಮಣ್ಯ ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನ","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kannur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":78.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Shrivagilu railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":20.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"f65771d1-437e-4bde-bc48-be626e43d040","name":"Bhimakali Temple, Sarahan","deity":"Bhimakali (Devi)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Himachal Pradesh","district":"Shimla","town":"Sarahan","latitude":31.44943,"longitude":77.63087,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Sutlej River","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":"Navratri and Dussehra are the major festivals.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T08:39:44.697229+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Traditionally the tutelary temple of the former Bushahr princely state's ruling family, and regarded by tradition as one of the 51 Shakti Peethas. Sources place its origin around the 13th century, though that date is approximate rather than inscription-fixed. The temple survived the 1905 Kangra earthquake — its main tower reportedly tilted and was later straightened — and underwent major reconstruction under Raja Padam Singh in the 1920s.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Bhuntar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":65.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Shimla railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":59.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia; Bushahr state tradition","architecture_style":"Kath-Kuni style (alternating timber-and-stone construction), twin towers, three courtyards","construction_century":13},{"id":"f6624e31-a395-424b-9205-55e957e3c5ba","name":"Uthirakosamangai","deity":"Shiva as Mangalanathar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Ramanathapuram","town":"Ramanathapuram","latitude":9.31667,"longitude":78.73333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vaigai River","river_distance_km":13.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:59.708182+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple near Ramanathapuram, Tamil Nadu, also called Mangalanatha Swamy temple, spread over about 20 acres. Its main shrines are those of Mangalanathar, Mangalambigai and Natarajar, and it holds a 6 ft emerald Nataraja image described as unique. Six daily rituals are held between 5:30 a.m. and 8 p.m., and the state endowment board runs it.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Six daily rituals are performed between 5:30 a.m. and 8 p.m.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_