Bahadur Singh, the temple encloses a natural cave-like rock formation where Hidimba is said to have meditated; there is no carved idol in the main sanctum, only a footprint relic and a small brass image. The underlying legend is itself from the Mahabharata — Hidimba, a Rakshasi, married the Pandava Bhima here and bore their son Ghatotkacha — epic tradition rather than verifiable history, distinct from the temple structure's own well-attested 16th-century construction date.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Bhuntar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":40.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Joginder Nagar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":46.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia; temple records","architecture_style":"Wooden pagoda-style shikhara — a roughly 24m tiered timber tower with an elaborately carved wooden doorway","construction_century":16},{"id":"fc2d648b-fce5-4a5b-b6e8-812cc193fad1","name":"Kolanjiappar temple","deity":"Murugan","sampradaya":"Kaumara","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Cuddalore","town":"Virudhachalam","latitude":11.52194,"longitude":79.29972,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Manimutha River","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:13:52.370722+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Murugan temple at Manavalanallur near Virudhachalam, Cuddalore district, in Dravidian style with a five-tiered gateway tower and pillared hall. Its legend is tied to t